26. a-di be-le-su2-nu ba-al-t,a3-at mi-im-ma!(mu)-sza
#tr.ts: adi bēle(s)sunu balṭat mimmâša
#tr.en: As long as Bēlessunu lives, her property

27. qa2-ti {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu-ma u2-ka-al-ma
#tr.ts: qāti amat-māmūma ukālma
#tr.en: Amat-šamaš will hold and

28. i-na _mu 1(disz)-kam 6(asz) sze gur 1(u) 2(disz) ma-na siki-hi-a <2(ban2)> 4(disz) [sila3 i3-ba_]
#tr.ts: ina ištēt šattim šeššet kur še’am šinšeret manā šīpātim šitta šât ešret qa piššatam
#tr.en: every year: 1.800 litres of barley, 12 minas of wool allowance, 24 litres of oil allotment,

29. 6(disz) ezem-hi-a 2(ban2) zi3-da-ta-a u3 2(disz) uzu-ta-a#_
#tr.ts: šeššet isinnī šitta šât qēmam u šinā šīrī
#tr.en: 6 "isinnu" food portions, 20 litres of flour and 2 thigh-cuts of meat,

30. {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu a-na be-le-su2-nu i-na-ad-di#-[isz-szi-im]
#tr.ts: amat-māmu ana bēle(s)sunu inaddiššim
#tr.en: Amat-māmu to Bēlessunu will provide her.

31. _2/3(disz) ma-na 6(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar_ hu-bu-li be-le-su2-nu
#tr.ts: šinip manā šeššet šiqil kaspam ḫubu(l)li bēle(s)sunu
#tr.en: 46 shekels of silver, a debt of Bēlessunu,

32. {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ {d}suen-dingir i-pu-ul
#tr.ts: amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilī īpul
#tr.en: Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī paid (so)

33. {disz}be-le-su2-nu u2-ul ih-ta-ba-al
#tr.ts: bēle(s)sunu ul iḫtabal
#tr.en: Bēlessunu is no (more) in debt.

34. mi-im-mu-sza an-nu-um a-na hu-bu-li-sza u2-ul iz-za-az
#tr.ts: mimmûša annûm ana ḫubu(l)līša ul izzaz
#tr.en: All her (aforementioned) property will not be liable for her debt (and)

35. sza sze-a-am u3 _ku3-babbar_ i-qi2-ip-pu-szi i-na mi-im-mu-sza# i-te-el-li
#tr.ts: ša še’am ū kaspam iqippūši ina mimmûša ītelli
#tr.en: whoever would lend barley or silver to her, would have no right to (lit. will forfeit) her property.

36. isz-tu be-le-su2-nu ap-lu-sa3 an-ni-tam
#tr.ts: ištu bēle(s)sunu aplū(s)sa annîtam
#tr.en: After Bēlessunu this inheritance

37. a-na a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu id-di-nu-ma _mu 2(disz)-kam_ i-pe2-ru-szi
#tr.ts: ana amat-māmu iddinūma šittā šanātim īpirūši
#tr.en: to Amat-māmu gave and supported her for two years,

38. {disz}geme2-{d}utu _dumu-munus_ i3-li2-i-qi2-sza-am u3 ni-szi-i-ni-szu _dumu-munus_ dingir-pi4-{d}utu
#tr.ts: amat-šamaš mārat ilī-iqīšam u nīši-īnīšu mārat anum-pî-šamaš
#tr.en: Amat-šamaš daughter of Ilī-iqīšam and Nīši-īnīšu daughter of Anum-pî-šamaš,

39. _dumu-munus-mesz_ ah-hi a-bi-sza a-na _a-sza3_ sza pi2-i t,up-pi2 an-ni-im
#tr.ts: mārāt aḫḫī abīša ana eqlim ša pî tuppi(m) annîm
#tr.en: her cousins, for the field(s) which are reported in this tablet,

40. a#-na# be-le-su2-nu ir-gu-ma-ma
#tr.ts: ana bēle(s)sunu irgumāma
#tr.en: raised a claim against Bēlessunu.

41. {disz}zi-im-ri-e-ra-ah ra-bi-a-an zimbir#{[ki]}
#tr.ts: zimri-eraḫ rabiān sippir
#tr.en: Zimri-eraḫ, the mayor of Sippar,

42. u3# _kar_ zimbir{ki} i-na _ka2_ {d}utu i#-mu#-ru#-[ma]
#tr.ts: u kār sippir ina bāb šamaš īmurūma
#tr.en: and the kārum body of Sippar investigated (the case) at the gate of Šamaš and:

43. t,up-pa-at nu-du-ne2-e be-le-su2-nu _lukur_ {d}utu
#tr.ts: ṭuppāt nudu(n)nê bēle(s)sunu nadīt šamaš
#tr.en: the tablets concerning the dowry of Bēlessunu nadītu of Šamaš,

44. sza a-bu-sza ma-la _sza3_-sza u2-sza-am-s,u2-u2-szi
#tr.ts: ša abūša mala libbīša ušamṣūši
#tr.en: which her father had conceded her full discretion over;

45. t,up#-pa#-at ap-lu-ut na-ra-am-tum a-ha-at a-bi-sza
#tr.ts: ṭuppāt aplūt narāmtum aḫat abīša
#tr.en: the inheritance tablets of Narāmtum her aunt,

46. [sza ap]-lu-sa3 id-di-nu-szi-im-ma
#tr.ts: ša aplū(s)sa iddinūšimma
#tr.en: who had given her inheritance to her and (who)

47. [e-ma] e#-li-sza t,a3-bu ap-lu-sa3 na-da-nam isz-t,u2-ru-szi
#tr.ts: ēma elīša ṭābu aplū(s)sa nadanam išṭurūši
#tr.en: had put in writing that she would place her inheritance wherever was good for her,

@reverse
